# SYNTHESIZED. Empty and whitespace-only lines are framing, not messages: a
# writer that flushes a bare newline has not asked for anything, and answering
# -32700 would fill the client's log with errors about nothing. Ignored in
# silence, and never mistaken for EOF (the loop keeps reading).
>
>
>
# Three spaces, spelled in base64 so no editor can silently trim them away.
>b64 ICAg
> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"ping"}
< {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"$keys": []}}
>
> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"method":"initialize","params":{"protocolVersion":"2025-06-18"}}
< {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18"}}
# Leading and trailing whitespace around a real message is tolerated too -- the
# line is stripped before parsing, so a pretty-printer's indentation does not
# become a protocol error.
>   {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"method":"ping"}
< {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "result": {"$keys": []}}
